+## Persistence and supported workload policy
+
+No durable pack state. All input settings/vectors are workflow-owned; outputs are render-local. Static arithmetic tables are immutable pack resources, not authored libraries/caches. Fresh filesystem/fresh guest proofs cover stateless reconstruction, not cloud KV durability.
+
+Coordinator-approved local safety policy, explicitly narrower than pristine input domains and NOT hard physical quotas:
+
+- Input integer magnitude <=2048 bits; projected output <=4096 bits.
+- Factorial <=512; absolute power exponent <=4096; shift count <=4096, with projected size checked BEFORE operation. Bool-as-int source intent and small negative/domain failures are retained.
+- FLOAT can consume actual Python ints from prior FLOAT Round nodes; integer expansion is preflighted there too, never silently coerced.
+- Vectors: exact flat tuple/list of 0..4 entries, including short/unequal admitted malformed shapes. Closed exact builtin/NumPy numeric scalar leaves, integer components <=2048 bits; no nested/object/string/structured arrays or arbitrary iterables. No padding, coercion or clamp. Structural/scalar checks precede NumPy allocation; fixed-size integer Dot has a conservative projected <=4096-bit result check.
+- Choice/resolution text <=128 characters before lookup/split/parsing. Inputs exceeding the envelope fail closed; no replacement math or hidden truncation.
